n433:        implementation_status:\n442:                \"spec complete\" means SRD, use case, and code exist (code at v1 tag). \"specs written\"\n443:                means SRD, use case, and test suite exist but code generation has not run yet.\n444:                \"pending\" means no SRD yet. See road-map.yaml for the active release and\n454:                - cmd/ls: specs written (rel02.0 core / rel02.1 extended) — SRD, use case, and test suite complete; code generation pending\n455:                - cmd/du: specs written (rel02.0) — SRD, use case, and test suite complete; code generation pending\n474:                Every cmd/ package verifies its implementation by running the Go binary and the\n533:                  status: implemented\n537:                  status: implemented\n541:                  status: implemented\n543:                  status: implemented\n545:                  status: implemented\n637:                due to task complexity from expanded sub-requirements.\n671:                Full ls implementation covering all flags: default, -1, -l, -a, -A, -d, --color, -h\n674:                merged after combining srd008-ls and srd010-ls-extended into a single SRD.\n1141:                layout. ptx produces a permuted keyword-in-context index. All SRDs have been\n1142:                restructured so each weight-4 requirement is in its own group. All are verified\n1165:                      specstatus: implemented\n1166:                      codestatus: implemented\n1175:                      specstatus: implemented\n1176:                      codestatus: implemented\n1185:                      specstatus: implemented\n1186:                      codestatus: implemented\n1190:                      specstatus: implemented\n1191:                      codestatus: implemented\n1195:                      specstatus: implemented\n1196:                      codestatus: implemented\n1212:                  codereadiness: all implemented\n1216:                