{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014JqXGGgEwvFPeVqSbhB4hW","type":"tool_result","content":"- index: 0\n  title: srd002-sys -- pkg/sys (contract)\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd002-sys.yaml (full SRD for pkg/sys)\n      - CLAUDE.md (SIGPIPE handling pattern and project conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo.go\n        action: create\n        note: FileInfo struct and Stat/Lstat function stubs\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: TerminalWidth and IsTerminal function stubs\n      - path: pkg/sys/signal.go\n        action: create\n        note: InstallSIGPIPEHandler and OnTerminalResize function stubs\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define FileInfo struct with fields: Mode os.FileMode, Size int64, Nlink uint64, Uid uint32, Gid uint32, Rdev uint64, Dev uint64, Ino uint64, Blocks int64, Blksize int64, ModTime time.Time, AccessTime time.Time, ChangeTime time.Time, Info os.FileInfo\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define file metadata function signatures as stubs: Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error), Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define terminal function signatures as stubs: TerminalWidth() (int, error), IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Define signal function signatures as stubs: InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Split exports across three files by domain: fileinfo.go (struct and stat functions), terminal.go (terminal queries), signal.go (signal handlers)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Package must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Stub functions must compile on Darwin -- use placeholder return values (nil, zero, etc.) so go build passes\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/ compiles: go build ./pkg/sys/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All exported types and functions match the signatures specified in R1-R4\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/... passes with no errors\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No imports of cmd/ or other pkg/ packages\"\n  dependency: -1\n- index: 1\n  title: srd001-testutils -- pkg/testutils (contract)\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml (full SRD for pkg/testutils)\n      - CLAUDE.md (differential testing pattern and BuildBinary usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: create\n        note: All exported types and function signatures as compilable Go stubs\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define DiffTest struct with fields: Name string, Args []string, Stdin []byte, Env []string, WorkDir string, ExitCode int, Normalize []NormalizeFunc, ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define NormalizeFunc type alias: type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define function signatures as stubs: RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest), ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc, BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Define TimestampNormalizer as a package-level var of type NormalizeFunc with a placeholder implementation\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary source file is difftest.go, named after the primary exported type DiffTest\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Package must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Stub functions must compile -- use t.Fatal('not implemented') or return zero values so go build passes\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"BuildBinary compiles a cmd/ package from within the Go module and returns the path to the built binary -- include it in the contract per the differential testing shared protocol in CLAUDE.md\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest.go exists and compiles: go build ./pkg/testutils/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All exported types and functions match the signatures specified in R1-R4\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no errors\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No imports of cmd/ or other pkg/ packages\"\n  dependency: -1\n- index: 2\n  title: srd002-sys R1.1-R1.4 -- FileInfo struct and Stat/Lstat implementation\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd002-sys.yaml (requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (contract stubs from prior task)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01PbWyee27em6Vc9uL128A29","session_id":"8712a2a4-759f-4848-9d0f-c286fe0a86e4","uuid":"05a6eda8-c3a3-4d36-8bb0-10f14f54b6e1","timestamp":"2026-05-23T02:03:24.095Z"}
