{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5502) for generation-run44 in the go-unix-utils project. This is an automated code generation pipeline where Claude implements Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities based on formal SRD specifications. The task is on branch `task/generation-run44-5502`. The previous task (#5501) implemented sha384sum (srd075 R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3). The task prompt includes massive project context (VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, ROADMAP, all pkg/ source code, execution constitution, Go style guide, requirement states, shared protocols, and package contracts). The task description states: \"Cobbler measure is calling Claude to propose task 0 for generation generation-run44.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries\n   - Cobbler-scaffold pipeline: measure (task planning) → stitch (code generation)\n   - SRDs (Software Requirements Documents) with numbered requirements as source of truth\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs GNU reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handler requirement for all cmd/ utilities via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - `exec.LookPath` + `t.Skip` pattern for graceful handling of missing reference binaries\n   - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` for compiling cmd/ packages within the Go module\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for all differential tests\n   - Shared pkg/ libraries: testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil\n   - Generation run 44 is the current active generation\n   - max_requirements_per_task: 4 (weight budget constraint)\n   - Execution constitution wit